; PointerCensus.scaly - the `--pointer-report` pass: every use of a raw
; `pointer[T]` in a compilation root, classified off the PLAN rather than off
; the source text.
;
; WHY A PLAN PASS. The pointer→ref campaign ran on Python text scans, and every
; class those scans got wrong was a question the Planner had already answered:
; a cast is a declaration without a colon; `p[i]` is arithmetic on a
; `pointer[Array[X]]` and a dispatch on a `ref[Array[X]]`; a `Slice` handed to a
; `pointer` parameter compiles silently; which SIDE of a `set` an occurrence is
; on. This pass reads the resolved types and reports one line per site, so a
; residue number is a MEASUREMENT that can be re-run, not a figure inherited
; from a scan whose population nobody checked.
;
; WHAT IT REPORTS (one line each, `<class> <detail>`, located file:line:col
; by the cli like `--task-plan`):
;   extern-param / extern-return   a pointer in an `extern` declaration
;   param / return / field / variant / local
;                                  a pointer in a declared position
;   deref                          `*p` on a pointer (a `*` on `ref[T]?` is
;                                  the language's Option spelling and is
;                                  COUNTED, never listed)
;   deref-arith                    `*(p + i)` -- the buffer walk
;   arith                          `p + i` / `p - i` as a value
;       The three buffer-walk classes (deref-arith, store-arith, arith) carry
;       the PROVENANCE of the walked pointer and the length in reach:
;         base=param(p) len=n            a parameter; `n` is the first integer
;                                        parameter after it (else any, `len=n?`)
;         base=local(p<-alloc)           a local; after `<-` the KIND of its
;                                        initializer: alloc (allocate/malloc/
;                                        ...), stack[N] (`var b u8[N]`),
;                                        param(x), local(x), field(T.f),
;                                        call(f), deref, arith, addr, null, ...
;         base=field(T.f) len=T.n        a field read; `n` the first integer
;                                        sibling field whose name says length
;                                        (len/size/count/cap/n), else the first
;                                        integer sibling marked `len=T.n?`
;         base=call(f) recv=T len=T.n    a call result (`x.get_buffer() + i`);
;                                        the receiver concept and ITS length
;         base=global(g) / deref / arith / other
;       A `*(X.get_buffer() + i)` whose receiver KNOWS its length is `X.at(i)`
;       or `X[i]` waiting to be written; a `param` walk with a `len` beside it
;       is a `Slice`; a `local(p<-alloc)` walk is a candidate for
;       `allocate_slice`. The verdict is still READ at the site.
;   cast / null-cast               `x as pointer[T]` / `null as pointer[T]`
;   null-test                      `p = null` / `p <> null` on a pointer
;   store / store-arith            `set *p: v` / `set *(p + i): v`
;   arg                            a pointer handed to a callee whose parameter
;                                  is a pointer too -- the forwarder chain,
;                                  `-> callee(param)`
;   arg-extern                     a pointer on its way to an `extern` (class X
;                                  of the doctrine: the cast there is forced)
;   arg-unresolved                 a pointer handed to a callee the flat
;                                  function table does not hold (intrinsic,
;                                  indirect, cross-package)
;   h-pointer-into-ref             HAZARD: a pointer-shaped value reaching a
;                                  parameter declared `ref[T]` / `ref[T]?`
;                                  (the `null as pointer[X]` spelling class)
;   h-slice-into-pointer           HAZARD: a `Slice` handed to a `pointer`
;                                  parameter -- compiles, reads the struct
;   h-mixed-params                 a signature with both `ref` and `pointer`
;                                  parameters, one campaign's verdict on one
;                                  neighbour and none on the other
;   h-store-through-ref-slot       HAZARD: `set *(p + i): v` / `set *p: v` on a
;                                  `pointer[ref[X]]` whose source is a VALUE --
;                                  the planner rewrites the target into the
;                                  nested deref and copies the struct through
;                                  whatever pointer the slot holds, never INTO
;                                  the slot (measured 2026-09-05, `and_analyze1`).
;                                  A REFERENCE source rebinds the slot since
;                                  2026-09-14 (`operand_is_rebindable_target#`),
;                                  and so does the Option element
;                                  `pointer[ref[X]?]`: ordinary stores.
;
; The callee is read off `plan.functions` by `PlannedCall.mangled_name`; a
; call's args line up with the callee's `input` INCLUDING its `this`, which is
; why the receiver of a method call is never a site (the pointer-ness of a
; receiver local is counted at the local). Where a name is recorded twice a
; body wins over an extern stub (the lazy method hook records a stub first).
;
; WHAT IT DOES NOT DO. It never reads the emission and never asks whether a
; call type-checks -- `emit_call` synthesizes the callee type from the
; ARGUMENTS, so "it compiled" is not evidence here. It runs BEFORE the hard
; diagnostics gate (the `--use-vis` slot), so a half-converted root still
; measures; every ref in the plan is therefore tested for null before use.
;
; PROVENANCE. Declarations are walked over the MODEL (`Program.module_`):
; a `Module` carries its `file`, and the Model tree holds every declaration
; of THIS root exactly once, as written. The Plan cannot serve that half --
; `plan_namespace#` plans a namespace's sub-modules for their side effects
; only and leaves `PlannedNamespace.modules` null, so for a library root the
; planned module tree is empty; and a generic concept's methods appear in
; `plan.functions` once per instantiation, filed under the REQUESTING file.
; Reading the written type also means a TYPE ALIAS (`define LLVMValueRef
; pointer[LLVMOpaqueValue]`) is NOT a pointer here -- the named handle is the
; accepted form, and only the alias's own definition line names a pointer.
; Bodies are walked over the flat `plan.functions`, whose
; `PlannedFunction.file` is the function's own module file. Report strings
; live on this pass's page (`String^this`), the `--task-plan` idiom: a
; default-local copy dangles by print time.
;
; SHAPE, NOT NAME. `ref[T]?` is `Option[ref[T]]` and `pointer[T]?` is
; `Option[pointer[T]]` (s113), so every shape question here peels the Option
; first. A `this` parameter is planned as `pointer[T]` by the Planner itself
; and is skipped by NAME -- it is the compiler's wrapper, not the author's.
;
; CONTROL-FLOW NOTE: `if COND STMT` runs STMT when COND is TRUE (no else).

use scalyc.compiler.Model.*
use scalyc.compiler.Plan.*
use scalyc.compiler.Planner.*
use scaly.os.File

; Dedupe table size: a power of two (the probe mask is DD_CAP - 1). The table
; stops admitting new keys at half load and every later site is recorded
; undeduplicated, so a root with more than 131072 sites still reports, only
; with instantiation duplicates past that point.
define DD_CAP int 262144

define PointerCensus
{
    define PointerCensus
    (
        ; One slot per reported site, in walk order: the owning file, the
        ; site's byte offset in that file, and the `<class> <detail>` text.
        report_files: Array[String]
        report_offsets: Array[size_t]
        report_texts: Array[String]

        ; Per-class counters for the head line.
        var n_extern: size_t
        var n_param: size_t
        var n_return: size_t
        var n_field: size_t
        var n_variant: size_t
        var n_local: size_t
        var n_deref: size_t
        var n_deref_arith: size_t
        var n_arith: size_t
        var n_cast: size_t
        var n_null_cast: size_t
        var n_null_test: size_t
        var n_store: size_t
        var n_arg: size_t
        ; `*opt` on a `ref[T]?` -- counted for calibration, never listed.
        var n_optref_deref: size_t
        ; Bodies whose `file` could not be verified nor re-derived (below);
        ; their sites are NOT reported, and the head line says how many.
        var n_unfiled: size_t

        ; Every module file of this root (collected on the Model walk) and
        ; its text, read on first use. `PlannedFunction.file` is the
        ; REQUESTING file for a lazily instantiated generic body, so before a
        ; body is walked its header is looked for at `loc.start` in that file
        ; (storelens.scaly's join), and on a miss in every other file of the
        ; root. Measured before this: 13 of 1875 stdlib sites filed under
        ; `containers.scaly`, the file that requested HashMap[String, int].
        src_files: Array[String]
        src_texts: Array[String]
        src_loaded: Array[size_t]

        ; Pointees of the root's TYPE ALIASES (`define LLVMValueRef
        ; pointer[LLVMOpaqueValue]` puts `LLVMOpaqueValue` here). The alias is
        ; resolved before planning, so in a BODY the handle arrives as
        ; `pointer[LLVMOpaqueValue]` and would be counted like any pointer;
        ; the named handle is the ACCEPTED form (one declaration per opaque
        ; kind), so such a site is COUNTED under `handle` and never listed.
        ; Measured before this: 7081 of scalyc's 9289 sites were LLVM handles.
        handle_pointees: Array[String]
        var n_handle: size_t

        ; Step 3: callee resolution. Open addressing over DD_CAP slots holding
        ; index + 1 into plan.functions, keyed by the mangled name's hash.
        var plan_functions: ref[Vector[PlannedFunction]]?
        fn_slots: Vector[size_t]
        ; Initializers live under plan.structures, not in plan.functions: a
        ; second table keyed the same way, holding (structure index << 16 |
        ; initializer index) + 1.
        var plan_structures: ref[Vector[PlannedStructure]]?
        init_slots: Vector[size_t]
        ; Every `extern` name of this root AND of its dependency packages
        ; (`Program.packages`): a dependency's extern has no entry in this
        ; root's plan.functions, so `memcpy` from the stdlib would otherwise
        ; read as unresolved.
        extern_names: Array[String]
        var n_arg_extern: size_t
        var n_arg_unresolved: size_t
        var n_h_ptr_ref: size_t
        var n_h_slice_ptr: size_t
        var n_h_mixed: size_t
        var n_h_store_slot: size_t

        ; Per-body context for the buffer-walk provenance (`base=`/`len=`):
        ; the parameters of the body being walked (null for the program's
        ; top-level statements), and every pointer-typed local recorded so
        ; far in this body with the KIND of its initializer (parallel arrays).
        var cur_params: ref[Vector[PlannedItem]]?
        var loc_names: Array[String]
        var loc_kinds: Array[String]

        ; Source file of the declaration or body currently walked.
        var current_file: String

        ; Dedupe over (file, offset, class). A generic concept's methods sit
        ; in plan.functions ONCE PER INSTANTIATION, all with the same file
        ; and offsets, so without this every site in a generic body counts
        ; as many times as the root instantiates it (`Vector.scaly:121`
        ; came out five times over the stdlib). Open addressing over
        ; DD_CAP slots holding site index + 1; the parallel arrays carry
        ; the key so a probe compares the whole triple.
        dd_slots: Vector[size_t]
        dd_hashes: Array[size_t]
        dd_offsets: Array[size_t]
        dd_classes: Array[size_t]
    )
    {
        init()
        {
            set report_files: Array[String]^this()
            set report_offsets: Array[size_t]^this()
            set report_texts: Array[String]^this()
            set n_extern: 0
            set n_param: 0
            set n_return: 0
            set n_field: 0
            set n_variant: 0
            set n_local: 0
            set n_deref: 0
            set n_deref_arith: 0
            set n_arith: 0
            set n_cast: 0
            set n_null_cast: 0
            set n_null_test: 0
            set n_store: 0
            set n_arg: 0
            set n_optref_deref: 0
            set n_unfiled: 0
            set current_file: String^this("")
            set src_files: Array[String]^this()
            set src_texts: Array[String]^this()
            set src_loaded: Array[size_t]^this()
            set handle_pointees: Array[String]^this()
            set n_handle: 0
            set plan_functions: null
            set fn_slots: Vector[size_t]^this(DD_CAP)
            set plan_structures: null
            set init_slots: Vector[size_t]^this(DD_CAP)
            set extern_names: Array[String]^this()
            set n_arg_extern: 0
            set n_arg_unresolved: 0
            set n_h_ptr_ref: 0
            set n_h_slice_ptr: 0
            set n_h_mixed: 0
            set n_h_store_slot: 0
            set cur_params: null
            set loc_names: Array[String]^this()
            set loc_kinds: Array[String]^this()
            set dd_slots: Vector[size_t]^this(DD_CAP)
            set dd_hashes: Array[size_t]^this()
            set dd_offsets: Array[size_t]^this()
            set dd_classes: Array[size_t]^this()
        }

        ; ================================================================
        ; Entry point: declarations over the module tree, then every
        ; planned body plus the program's top-level statements.
        ; ================================================================
        procedure analyze(mutable this: PointerCensus, plan: Plan, model: ref[Program], entry_file: String)
        {
            this.walk_model_module(model.module_)
            var pi: size_t 0
            while pi < model.packages.length
            {
                let pkg model.packages.get pi
                if pkg <> null
                    this.collect_externs_module((*pkg))
                set pi: pi + 1
            }
            set plan_functions: plan.functions
            set plan_structures: plan.structures
            this.index_functions()
            this.index_initializers()
            if plan.functions <> null
            {
                for func in plan.functions
                {
                    choose func.impl
                        when action: Action
                        {
                            let home this.resolve_body_file(func)
                            if home.get_length() > 0
                            {
                                set current_file: String^this(home)
                                set cur_params: func.input
                                set loc_names: Array[String]^this()
                                set loc_kinds: Array[String]^this()
                                this.find_action(action)
                            }
                            else
                                set n_unfiled: n_unfiled + 1
                        }
                        else
                            0
                }
            }
            if plan.statements <> null
            {
                set current_file: String^this(entry_file)
                set cur_params: null
                set loc_names: Array[String]^this()
                set loc_kinds: Array[String]^this()
                for stmt in plan.statements
                    this.find_statement(stmt)
            }
        }

        function total(this: PointerCensus) returns size_t
            report_offsets.length

        ; ================================================================
        ; Type shape. Every question peels the s113 Option wrapper first.
        ; ================================================================

        ; The type under a one-argument `Option`, or the type itself.
        function peel_option(t: PlannedType) returns PlannedType
        {
            if t.name <> "Option"
                return t
            if t.generics = null
                return t
            let gens (*t.generics)
            if gens.length <> 1
                return t
            let inner_ptr gens.get 0
            if inner_ptr = null
                return t
            (*inner_ptr)
        }

        function void_type() returns PlannedType
            PlannedType(Span(0, 0), "void", "v", null, Lifetime.Unspecified(Unspecified()), null, "", null)

        ; `pointer[T]` or `pointer[T]?`.
        function is_pointer_shaped(t: PlannedType) returns bool
        {
            let core PointerCensus.peel_option(t)
            core.name = "pointer"
        }

        ; `ref[T]?` -- the one deref spelling that is the language's own.
        function is_optional_ref(t: PlannedType) returns bool
        {
            if t.name <> "Option"
                return false
            let core PointerCensus.peel_option(t)
            core.name = "ref"
        }

        ; A `pointer[X]` (or `pointer[X]?`) whose X is an alias pointee.
        function is_handle(this: PointerCensus, t: PlannedType) returns bool
        {
            let core PointerCensus.peel_option(t)
            if core.name <> "pointer"
                return false
            if core.generics = null
                return false
            if core.generics.length <> 1
                return false
            let inner core.generics.get 0
            if inner = null
                return false
            let pointee inner.unwrap().name
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < handle_pointees.length
            {
                let h handle_pointees.get i
                if h <> null and (*h) = pointee
                    return true
                set i: i + 1
            }
            false
        }

        ; The receiver the planner passes for a sibling method call: the
        ; `this` variable, planned as `pointer[T]` by the compiler itself.
        function operand_is_this(op: PlannedOperand) returns bool
        {
            if op.member_access <> null
                return false
            choose op.expr
                when v: Variable
                    return v.name = "this"
                else
                    return false
        }

        ; ================================================================
        ; Recording. `text` must ALREADY live on this pass's page -- every
        ; caller copies with `String^this(...)` before calling, because the
        ; escape checker reads a callee that stores its argument as storing
        ; the caller's LOCAL (it is field-insensitive and does not see that
        ; a copy inside would be made): "argument on the local page is
        ; stored beyond the frame by record".
        ; ================================================================
        procedure record(mutable this: PointerCensus, offset: size_t, cls: String, text: String)
        {
            let cid PointerCensus.class_id(cls)
            if this.dedupe_seen(offset, cid)
                return
            let file_copy String^this(current_file)
            report_files.add file_copy
            report_offsets.add offset
            report_texts.add text
            this.bump(cid)
        }

        ; Answers true when (current_file, offset, cid) was recorded before;
        ; otherwise inserts it and answers false.
        procedure dedupe_seen(mutable this: PointerCensus, offset: size_t, cid: size_t) returns bool
        {
            let fh current_file.hash()
            let mask (DD_CAP as size_t) - 1
            var h fh
            set h: h xor (offset * 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15)
            set h: h xor (cid * 0x100000001B3)
            set h: h & mask
            var probes: size_t 0
            while probes < mask
            {
                let slot_ptr dd_slots.get h
                if slot_ptr = null
                    return false
                let slot (*slot_ptr)
                if slot = 0
                {
                    if dd_hashes.length * 2 >= (DD_CAP as size_t)
                        return false
                    dd_slots.put(h, dd_hashes.length + 1)
                    dd_hashes.add fh
                    dd_offsets.add offset
                    dd_classes.add cid
                    return false
                }
                let idx slot - 1
                let ph dd_hashes.get idx
                let po dd_offsets.get idx
                let pc dd_classes.get idx
                if ph <> null and po <> null and pc <> null and (*ph) = fh and (*po) = offset and (*pc) = cid
                    return true
                set h: (h + 1) & mask
                set probes: probes + 1
            }
            false
        }

        function class_id(cls: String) returns size_t
        {
            if cls = "extern-param"
                return 1
            if cls = "extern-return"
                return 1
            if cls = "param"
                return 2
            if cls = "return"
                return 3
            if cls = "field"
                return 4
            if cls = "variant"
                return 5
            if cls = "local"
                return 6
            if cls = "deref"
                return 7
            if cls = "deref-arith"
                return 8
            if cls = "arith"
                return 9
            if cls = "cast"
                return 10
            if cls = "null-cast"
                return 11
            if cls = "null-test"
                return 12
            if cls = "store"
                return 13
            if cls = "store-arith"
                return 13
            if cls = "arg"
                return 14
            if cls = "arg-extern"
                return 15
            if cls = "arg-unresolved"
                return 16
            if cls = "h-pointer-into-ref"
                return 17
            if cls = "h-slice-into-pointer"
                return 18
            if cls = "h-mixed-params"
                return 19
            if cls = "h-store-through-ref-slot"
                return 20
            0
        }

        procedure bump(mutable this: PointerCensus, cid: size_t)
        {
            if cid = 1
                set n_extern: n_extern + 1
            if cid = 2
                set n_param: n_param + 1
            if cid = 3
                set n_return: n_return + 1
            if cid = 4
                set n_field: n_field + 1
            if cid = 5
                set n_variant: n_variant + 1
            if cid = 6
                set n_local: n_local + 1
            if cid = 7
                set n_deref: n_deref + 1
            if cid = 8
                set n_deref_arith: n_deref_arith + 1
            if cid = 9
                set n_arith: n_arith + 1
            if cid = 10
                set n_cast: n_cast + 1
            if cid = 11
                set n_null_cast: n_null_cast + 1
            if cid = 12
                set n_null_test: n_null_test + 1
            if cid = 13
                set n_store: n_store + 1
            if cid = 14
                set n_arg: n_arg + 1
            if cid = 15
                set n_arg_extern: n_arg_extern + 1
            if cid = 16
                set n_arg_unresolved: n_arg_unresolved + 1
            if cid = 17
                set n_h_ptr_ref: n_h_ptr_ref + 1
            if cid = 18
                set n_h_slice_ptr: n_h_slice_ptr + 1
            if cid = 19
                set n_h_mixed: n_h_mixed + 1
            if cid = 20
                set n_h_store_slot: n_h_store_slot + 1
        }

        procedure record_typed(mutable this: PointerCensus, offset: size_t, cls: String, t: PlannedType)
        {
            if this.is_handle(t)
            {
                set n_handle: n_handle + 1
                return
            }
            var sb StringBuilder()
            sb.append cls
            sb.append " "
            sb.append(Planner.get_readable_name(t))
            let text sb.to_string()
            let text_copy String^this(text)
            this.record(offset, cls, text_copy)
        }

        procedure record_named(mutable this: PointerCensus, offset: size_t, cls: String, t: PlannedType, name: String)
        {
            if this.is_handle(t)
            {
                set n_handle: n_handle + 1
                return
            }
            var sb StringBuilder()
            sb.append cls
            sb.append " "
            sb.append(Planner.get_readable_name(t))
            sb.append " "
            sb.append name
            let text sb.to_string()
            let text_copy String^this(text)
            this.record(offset, cls, text_copy)
        }

        ; ================================================================
        ; Declarations: the MODEL module tree carries the file.
        ; ================================================================

        ; Last segment of a Model type name (`scaly.memory.Page` -> `Page`).
        function model_last_segment(t: Type) returns String
        {
            if t.name.length = 0
                return ""
            let last t.name.get(t.name.length - 1)
            if last = null
                return ""
            String((*last))
        }

        ; `pointer[T]` or `pointer[T]?` as WRITTEN (s113 wraps `T?` into
        ; `Option[T]` at Model level, so the Option is peeled here too).
        function model_is_pointer(t: Type) returns bool
        {
            let last PointerCensus.model_last_segment(t)
            if last = "pointer"
                return true
            if last <> "Option"
                return false
            if t.generics = null
                return false
            if t.generics.length <> 1
                return false
            let inner t.generics.get 0
            if inner = null
                return false
            PointerCensus.model_is_pointer((*inner))
        }

        ; Readable rendering of a Model type: `a.b.Name[T, U]`.
        function model_type_name(t: Type) returns String
        {
            var sb StringBuilder()
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < t.name.length
            {
                if i > 0
                    sb.append "."
                let seg t.name.get i
                if seg <> null
                    sb.append((*seg))
                set i: i + 1
            }
            if t.generics <> null
            {
                sb.append "["
                var g: size_t 0
                while g < t.generics.length
                {
                    if g > 0
                        sb.append ", "
                    let gt t.generics.get g
                    if gt <> null
                        sb.append(PointerCensus.model_type_name((*gt)))
                    set g: g + 1
                }
                sb.append "]"
            }
            sb.to_string()
        }

        procedure record_model_typed(mutable this: PointerCensus, offset: size_t, cls: String, t: Type, name: String)
        {
            var sb StringBuilder()
            sb.append cls
            sb.append " "
            sb.append(PointerCensus.model_type_name(t))
            sb.append " "
            sb.append name
            let text sb.to_string()
            let text_copy String^this(text)
            this.record(offset, cls, text_copy)
        }

        procedure walk_model_module(mutable this: PointerCensus, m: Module)
        {
            set current_file: String^this(m.file)
            this.remember_file(m.file)
            this.walk_members(m.members)
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < m.modules.length
            {
                let sub m.modules.get i
                if sub <> null
                    this.walk_model_module((*sub))
                set i: i + 1
            }
            ; Restore: a sibling walked after this one belongs to ITS file,
            ; and the caller's remaining members to the caller's.
            set current_file: String^this(m.file)
        }

        procedure walk_members(mutable this: PointerCensus, members: Vector[Member])
        {
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < members.length
            {
                let m_ptr members.get i
                if m_ptr <> null
                {
                    let mem (*m_ptr)
                    choose mem
                        when f: Function
                            this.walk_model_function(f)
                        when o: Operator
                            this.walk_model_signature(o.input, o.returns_, false, o.name, o.span.start)
                        when c: Concept
                            this.walk_model_concept(c)
                        else
                            0
                }
                set i: i + 1
            }
        }

        procedure walk_model_function(mutable this: PointerCensus, f: Function)
        {
            var is_extern false
            choose f.implementation
                when e: Extern
                    set is_extern: true
                else
                    0
            if is_extern
                this.remember_extern(f.name)
            this.walk_model_signature(f.input, f.returns_, is_extern, f.name, f.span.start)
        }

        procedure remember_extern(mutable this: PointerCensus, name: String)
        {
            let copy String^this(name)
            extern_names.add copy
        }

        function is_extern_name(this: PointerCensus, name: String) returns bool
        {
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < extern_names.length
            {
                let e extern_names.get i
                if e <> null and (*e) = name
                    return true
                set i: i + 1
            }
            false
        }

        ; Dependency packages: only their extern NAMES are wanted.
        procedure collect_externs_module(mutable this: PointerCensus, m: Module)
        {
            this.collect_externs_members(m.members)
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < m.modules.length
            {
                let sub m.modules.get i
                if sub <> null
                    this.collect_externs_module((*sub))
                set i: i + 1
            }
        }

        procedure collect_externs_members(mutable this: PointerCensus, members: Vector[Member])
        {
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < members.length
            {
                let m_ptr members.get i
                if m_ptr <> null
                {
                    let mem (*m_ptr)
                    choose mem
                        when f: Function
                        {
                            choose f.implementation
                                when e: Extern
                                    this.remember_extern(f.name)
                                else
                                    0
                        }
                        when c: Concept
                        {
                            choose c.definition
                                when st: Structure
                                {
                                    this.collect_externs_members(st.members)
                                    var mi: size_t 0
                                    while mi < st.modules.length
                                    {
                                        let sub st.modules.get mi
                                        if sub <> null
                                            this.collect_externs_module((*sub))
                                        set mi: mi + 1
                                    }
                                }
                                when un: Union
                                    this.collect_externs_members(un.members)
                                when ns: Namespace
                                {
                                    this.collect_externs_members(ns.members)
                                    var mi: size_t 0
                                    while mi < ns.modules.length
                                    {
                                        let sub ns.modules.get mi
                                        if sub <> null
                                            this.collect_externs_module((*sub))
                                        set mi: mi + 1
                                    }
                                }
                                else
                                    0
                        }
                        else
                            0
                }
                set i: i + 1
            }
        }

        ; `ref[T]` or `ref[T]?` as written.
        function model_is_ref(t: Type) returns bool
        {
            let last PointerCensus.model_last_segment(t)
            if last = "ref"
                return true
            if last <> "Option"
                return false
            if t.generics = null
                return false
            if t.generics.length <> 1
                return false
            let inner t.generics.get 0
            if inner = null
                return false
            PointerCensus.model_is_ref((*inner))
        }

        procedure walk_model_signature(
            mutable this: PointerCensus,
            input: Vector[Item],
            returns_: ref[Type]?,
            is_extern: bool,
            owner: String,
            owner_off: size_t
        )
        {
            var n_ptr: size_t 0
            var n_ref: size_t 0
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < input.length
            {
                let item_ptr input.get i
                if item_ptr <> null
                {
                    let item (*item_ptr)
                    var is_this false
                    if item.name <> null
                    {
                        if (*item.name) = "this"
                            set is_this: true
                    }
                    if is_this = false
                    {
                        if item.type <> null
                        {
                            let t (*item.type)
                            if PointerCensus.model_is_ref(t)
                                set n_ref: n_ref + 1
                            if PointerCensus.model_is_pointer(t)
                            {
                                set n_ptr: n_ptr + 1
                                var pname String("")
                                if item.name <> null
                                    set pname: String((*item.name))
                                var sb StringBuilder()
                                sb.append owner
                                sb.append "("
                                sb.append pname
                                sb.append ")"
                                let where sb.to_string()
                                if is_extern
                                {
                                    this.record_model_typed(item.span.start, "extern-param", t, where)
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    this.record_model_typed(item.span.start, "param", t, where)
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
                set i: i + 1
            }
            ; The signpost of a half-converted routine: one campaign's verdict
            ; on one parameter and none on its neighbour.
            if is_extern = false
                if n_ptr > 0
                    if n_ref > 0
                    {
                        var sb StringBuilder()
                        sb.append "h-mixed-params "
                        sb.append owner
                        let text sb.to_string()
                        let text_copy String^this(text)
                        this.record(owner_off, "h-mixed-params", text_copy)
                    }
            if returns_ <> null
            {
                let rt (*returns_)
                if PointerCensus.model_is_pointer(rt)
                {
                    if is_extern
                    {
                        this.record_model_typed(rt.span.start, "extern-return", rt, owner)
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        this.record_model_typed(rt.span.start, "return", rt, owner)
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        procedure walk_model_concept(mutable this: PointerCensus, c: Concept)
        {
            choose c.definition
                when s: Structure
                {
                    var i: size_t 0
                    while i < s.properties.length
                    {
                        let p_ptr s.properties.get i
                        if p_ptr <> null
                        {
                            let p (*p_ptr)
                            if p.type <> null
                            {
                                let pt (*p.type)
                                if PointerCensus.model_is_pointer(pt)
                                {
                                    var sb StringBuilder()
                                    sb.append c.name
                                    sb.append "."
                                    sb.append p.name
                                    let where sb.to_string()
                                    this.record_model_typed(p.span.start, "field", pt, where)
                                }
                            }
                        }
                        set i: i + 1
                    }
                    var ii: size_t 0
                    while ii < s.initializers.length
                    {
                        let ini_ptr s.initializers.get ii
                        if ini_ptr <> null
                        {
                            let ini (*ini_ptr)
                            this.walk_model_signature(ini.input, null, false, c.name, ini.span.start)
                        }
                        set ii: ii + 1
                    }
                    this.walk_members(s.members)
                    var mi: size_t 0
                    while mi < s.modules.length
                    {
                        let sub s.modules.get mi
                        if sub <> null
                            this.walk_model_module((*sub))
                        set mi: mi + 1
                    }
                }
                when u: Union
                {
                    var i: size_t 0
                    while i < u.variants.length
                    {
                        let v_ptr u.variants.get i
                        if v_ptr <> null
                        {
                            let v (*v_ptr)
                            if v.type <> null
                            {
                                let vt (*v.type)
                                if PointerCensus.model_is_pointer(vt)
                                {
                                    var sb StringBuilder()
                                    sb.append c.name
                                    sb.append "."
                                    sb.append v.name
                                    let where sb.to_string()
                                    this.record_model_typed(v.span.start, "variant", vt, where)
                                }
                            }
                        }
                        set i: i + 1
                    }
                    this.walk_members(u.members)
                }
                when alias: Type
                {
                    ; `define Name pointer[X]`: remember X as a handle pointee.
                    if PointerCensus.model_last_segment(alias) = "pointer"
                    {
                        if alias.generics <> null
                        {
                            if alias.generics.length = 1
                            {
                                let inner alias.generics.get 0
                                if inner <> null
                                {
                                    let pointee PointerCensus.model_last_segment((*inner))
                                    let copy String^this(pointee)
                                    handle_pointees.add copy
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
                when ns: Namespace
                {
                    this.walk_members(ns.members)
                    var mi: size_t 0
                    while mi < ns.modules.length
                    {
                        let sub ns.modules.get mi
                        if sub <> null
                            this.walk_model_module((*sub))
                        set mi: mi + 1
                    }
                }
                else
                    0
        }

        ; ================================================================
        ; Callee lookup by mangled name.
        ; ================================================================
        function fn_is_body(f: PlannedFunction) returns bool
        {
            choose f.impl
                when action: Action
                    return true
                else
                    return false
        }

        procedure index_functions(mutable this: PointerCensus)
        {
            if plan_functions = null
                return
            let mask (DD_CAP as size_t) - 1
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < plan_functions.length
            {
                if i * 2 >= (DD_CAP as size_t)
                    return
                let f_ptr plan_functions.get i
                if f_ptr <> null
                {
                    let f (*f_ptr)
                    var h f.mangled_name.hash() & mask
                    var probes: size_t 0
                    var done false
                    while done = false
                    {
                        if probes >= mask
                            set done: true
                        if done = false
                        {
                            let slot_ptr fn_slots.get h
                            if slot_ptr = null
                                set done: true
                            if done = false
                            {
                                let slot (*slot_ptr)
                                if slot = 0
                                {
                                    fn_slots.put(h, i + 1)
                                    set done: true
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    let other plan_functions.get(slot - 1)
                                    if other <> null
                                    {
                                        if other.unwrap().mangled_name = f.mangled_name
                                        {
                                            ; Same symbol twice: a body beats a stub.
                                            if PointerCensus.fn_is_body(f)
                                                fn_slots.put(h, i + 1)
                                            set done: true
                                        }
                                    }
                                    if done = false
                                    {
                                        set h: (h + 1) & mask
                                        set probes: probes + 1
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
                set i: i + 1
            }
        }

        procedure index_initializers(mutable this: PointerCensus)
        {
            if plan_structures = null
                return
            let mask (DD_CAP as size_t) - 1
            var si: size_t 0
            while si < plan_structures.length
            {
                let s_ptr plan_structures.get si
                if s_ptr <> null
                {
                    let st s_ptr.unwrap()
                    if st.initializers <> null
                    {
                        var ii: size_t 0
                        while ii < st.initializers.length
                        {
                            let in_ptr st.initializers.get ii
                            if in_ptr <> null
                            {
                                let ini in_ptr.unwrap()
                                var h ini.mangled_name.hash() & mask
                                var probes: size_t 0
                                var done false
                                while done = false
                                {
                                    if probes >= mask
                                        set done: true
                                    if done = false
                                    {
                                        let slot_ptr init_slots.get h
                                        if slot_ptr = null
                                            set done: true
                                        if done = false
                                        {
                                            if (*slot_ptr) = 0
                                            {
                                                if si < 65536 and ii < 65536
                                                    init_slots.put(h, (si * 65536) + ii + 1)
                                                set done: true
                                            }
                                            else
                                            {
                                                set h: (h + 1) & mask
                                                set probes: probes + 1
                                            }
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                            set ii: ii + 1
                        }
                    }
                }
                set si: si + 1
            }
        }

        function find_initializer(this: PointerCensus, mangled: String) returns ref[PlannedInitializer]?
        {
            if plan_structures = null
                return null
            if mangled.get_length() = 0
                return null
            let mask (DD_CAP as size_t) - 1
            var h mangled.hash() & mask
            var probes: size_t 0
            while probes < mask
            {
                let slot_ptr init_slots.get h
                if slot_ptr = null
                    return null
                let slot (*slot_ptr)
                if slot = 0
                    return null
                let si (slot - 1) / 65536
                let ii (slot - 1) % 65536
                let s_ptr plan_structures.get si
                if s_ptr <> null
                {
                    let st s_ptr.unwrap()
                    if st.initializers <> null
                    {
                        let in_ptr st.initializers.get ii
                        if in_ptr <> null and in_ptr.unwrap().mangled_name = mangled
                            return in_ptr
                    }
                }
                set h: (h + 1) & mask
                set probes: probes + 1
            }
            null
        }

        function find_function(this: PointerCensus, mangled: String) returns ref[PlannedFunction]?
        {
            if plan_functions = null
                return null
            if mangled.get_length() = 0
                return null
            let mask (DD_CAP as size_t) - 1
            var h mangled.hash() & mask
            var probes: size_t 0
            while probes < mask
            {
                let slot_ptr fn_slots.get h
                if slot_ptr = null
                    return null
                let slot (*slot_ptr)
                if slot = 0
                    return null
                let cand plan_functions.get(slot - 1)
                if cand <> null and cand.unwrap().mangled_name = mangled
                    return cand
                set h: (h + 1) & mask
                set probes: probes + 1
            }
            null
        }

        ; Is `op` a `*q` whose `q` is a `pointer[ref[X]]` (plain or `q + i`)?
        function operand_is_deref_of_ref_slot(op: PlannedOperand) returns bool
        {
            if op.member_access <> null
                return false
            choose op.expr
                when call: Call
                {
                    if call.name <> "*"
                        return false
                    if call.args = null
                        return false
                    if call.args.length <> 1
                        return false
                    let q call.args.get 0
                    if q = null
                        return false
                    let qv q.unwrap()
                    let inner_args PointerCensus.arith_args(qv)
                    if inner_args <> null
                    {
                        let base inner_args.get 0
                        if base = null
                            return false
                        return PointerCensus.is_ref_slot_pointer(base.unwrap().result_type)
                    }
                    PointerCensus.is_ref_slot_pointer(qv.result_type)
                }
                else
                    return false
        }

        ; Walk the children of the slot pointer under `*q` / `*(q + i)`.
        procedure walk_below_deref(mutable this: PointerCensus, op: PlannedOperand)
        {
            choose op.expr
                when call: Call
                {
                    if call.args = null
                        return
                    let q call.args.get 0
                    if q = null
                        return
                    let qv q.unwrap()
                    let inner_args PointerCensus.arith_args(qv)
                    if inner_args <> null
                        this.find_operands(inner_args)
                    else
                        this.find_operand(qv)
                }
                else
                    0
        }

        ; The slot pointer's type under such a deref (for the report line).
        function deref_slot_type(op: PlannedOperand) returns PlannedType
        {
            choose op.expr
                when call: Call
                {
                    let q call.args.get 0
                    let qv q.unwrap()
                    let inner_args PointerCensus.arith_args(qv)
                    if inner_args <> null
                    {
                        let base inner_args.get 0
                        return base.unwrap().result_type
                    }
                    return qv.result_type
                }
                else
                    return PointerCensus.void_type()
        }

        ; `pointer[ref[X]]` (or `pointer[ref[X]]?`): a slot whose pointee is a
        ; NON-optional reference. `pointer[ref[X]?]` is deliberately excluded:
        ; a store into an Option slot rebinds.
        function is_ref_slot_pointer(t: PlannedType) returns bool
        {
            let core PointerCensus.peel_option(t)
            if core.name <> "pointer"
                return false
            if core.generics = null
                return false
            if core.generics.length <> 1
                return false
            let inner core.generics.get 0
            if inner = null
                return false
            inner.unwrap().name = "ref"
        }

        ; `ref[T]` or `ref[T]?` in the plan.
        function is_ref_shaped(t: PlannedType) returns bool
        {
            let core PointerCensus.peel_option(t)
            core.name = "ref"
        }

        ; ================================================================
        ; Source files: the join that verifies a body's file.
        ; ================================================================
        procedure remember_file(mutable this: PointerCensus, file: String)
        {
            if file.get_length() = 0
                return
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < src_files.length
            {
                let f src_files.get i
                if f <> null and (*f) = file
                    return
                set i: i + 1
            }
            let copy String^this(file)
            src_files.add copy
            let empty String^this("")
            src_texts.add empty
            src_loaded.add 0
        }

        ; The text of the i-th remembered file, read on first use.
        procedure source_of(mutable this: PointerCensus, i: size_t) returns ref[String]?
        {
            let loaded src_loaded.get i
            if loaded = null
                return null
            if (*loaded) = 0
            {
                let f src_files.get i
                if f = null
                    return null
                let text File.read_to_string((*f))
                let copy String^this(text)
                src_texts.put(i, copy)
                src_loaded.put(i, 1)
            }
            src_texts.get i
        }

        ; Does `src` read `lit` at offset `off`?
        function text_at(src: String, off: size_t, lit: String) returns bool
        {
            let n lit.get_length()
            if off + n > src.get_length()
                return false
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < n
            {
                if src.get(off + i) <> lit.get(i)
                    return false
                set i: i + 1
            }
            true
        }

        ; A routine header at `off`: one of the four keywords, then the
        ; routine's own name after the blanks. A lambda body has a synthetic
        ; name and starts at its backslash.
        function header_at(src: String, off: size_t, name: String) returns bool
        {
            if PointerCensus.text_at(src, off, "\\")
                return true
            var kw_len: size_t 0
            if PointerCensus.text_at(src, off, "function")
                set kw_len: 8
            if PointerCensus.text_at(src, off, "procedure")
                set kw_len: 9
            if PointerCensus.text_at(src, off, "operator")
                set kw_len: 8
            if PointerCensus.text_at(src, off, "init")
                set kw_len: 4
            if kw_len = 0
                return false
            if kw_len = 4
                return true
            var p off + kw_len
            let len src.get_length()
            while p < len
            {
                let c src.get p
                if c <> 32 and c <> 9
                    break
                set p: p + 1
            }
            PointerCensus.text_at(src, p, name)
        }

        ; The file a body was WRITTEN in: its own `file` when the header
        ; checks out there, else the one remembered file where it does, else
        ; the empty string. A body from a DEPENDENCY package (a stdlib generic
        ; instantiated by this root) names a file outside this root's module
        ; tree; it is remembered here on first sight, so its sites are
        ; reported under their true file and the sweep's union dedupes them.
        procedure resolve_body_file(mutable this: PointerCensus, func: PlannedFunction) returns String
        {
            this.remember_file(func.file)
            var i: size_t 0
            var own: size_t src_files.length
            while i < src_files.length
            {
                let f src_files.get i
                if f <> null and (*f) = func.file
                    set own: i
                set i: i + 1
            }
            if own < src_files.length
            {
                let src this.source_of(own)
                if src <> null and PointerCensus.header_at((*src), func.loc.start, func.name)
                    return String(func.file)
            }
            set i: 0
            while i < src_files.length
            {
                if i <> own
                {
                    let src this.source_of(i)
                    if src <> null
                        if PointerCensus.header_at((*src), func.loc.start, func.name)
                        {
                            let f src_files.get i
                            if f <> null
                                return String((*f))
                        }
                }
                set i: i + 1
            }
            String("")
        }

        ; ================================================================
        ; Bodies: the TaskPlanner's closed arm list, with the sites read
        ; off each operand before its children are walked.
        ; ================================================================

        procedure find_operands(mutable this: PointerCensus, ops: ref[Vector[PlannedOperand]]?)
        {
            if ops = null
                return
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < ops.length
            {
                let op_ptr ops.get i
                if op_ptr <> null
                    this.find_operand(op_ptr.unwrap())
                set i: i + 1
            }
        }

        procedure find_statement_ref(mutable this: PointerCensus, stmt: ref[PlannedStatement]?)
        {
            if stmt <> null
            {
                let s stmt
                this.find_statement((*s))
            }
        }

        ; A `set` whose target is a deref is a store THROUGH a pointer --
        ; the side of a `set` no text scan could tell apart.
        procedure find_action(mutable this: PointerCensus, act: PlannedAction)
        {
            this.find_operands(act.source)
            if act.target = null
                return
            var handled false
            if act.target.length > 0
            {
                let head_ptr act.target.get 0
                if head_ptr <> null
                {
                    let head (*head_ptr)
                    set handled: this.note_store_target(head)
                }
            }
            if handled = false
                this.find_operands(act.target)
        }

        ; Answers true when the target head is a store through a pointer and
        ; has been reported (and its children walked) here.
        procedure note_store_target(mutable this: PointerCensus, head: PlannedOperand) returns bool
        {
            if head.member_access <> null
                return false
            choose head.expr
                when call: Call
                {
                    if call.name <> "*"
                        return false
                    if call.args = null
                        return false
                    if call.args.length <> 1
                        return false
                    let a_ptr call.args.get 0
                    if a_ptr = null
                        return false
                    let a (*a_ptr)
                    ; The planner REWRITES a set target whose type is a ref into
                    ; the deref (`set_target_stores_through#`), so a store into a
                    ; `pointer[ref[X]]` slot arrives here as `*(*(p + i))` or
                    ; `*(*p)`: a deref whose argument is itself a deref of the
                    ; slot pointer. That nesting IS the hazard.
                    if PointerCensus.operand_is_deref_of_ref_slot(a)
                    {
                        this.record_typed(head.loc.start, "h-store-through-ref-slot", PointerCensus.deref_slot_type(a))
                        ; ONE site: walk below the slot pointer, not the inner deref.
                        this.walk_below_deref(a)
                        return true
                    }
                    let inner_args PointerCensus.arith_args(a)
                    if inner_args <> null
                    {
                        let base inner_args.get 0
                        if base <> null
                        {
                            ; a store into a ref slot that the planner did NOT rewrite
                            ; into the nested deref rebinds the slot (2026-09-14): an
                            ; ordinary store
                            this.record_walk(head.loc.start, "store-arith", base.unwrap())
                        }
                        this.find_operands(inner_args)
                        return true
                    }
                    if PointerCensus.is_pointer_shaped(a.result_type)
                    {
                        this.record_typed(head.loc.start, "store", a.result_type)
                        this.find_operand(a)
                        return true
                    }
                    return false
                }
                else
                    return false
        }

        procedure find_statement(mutable this: PointerCensus, stmt: PlannedStatement)
        {
            choose stmt
                when action: Action
                    this.find_action(action)
                when binding: Binding
                {
                    this.note_binding(binding)
                    this.find_operands(binding.operation)
                }
                when ret: Return
                    this.find_operands(ret.result)
                when throw_stmt: Throw
                    this.find_operands(throw_stmt.result)
                when brk: Break
                    this.find_operands(brk.result)
                when cont: Continue
                    0
        }

        ; A local whose (declared or inferred) type is a pointer. This is
        ; where `let p allocate(...) as pointer[X]` surfaces -- the cast that
        ; is a declaration without a colon.
        procedure note_binding(mutable this: PointerCensus, binding: PlannedBinding)
        {
            var have_type false
            var t: PlannedType PointerCensus.void_type()
            if binding.binding_item.item_type <> null
            {
                set t: (*binding.binding_item.item_type)
                set have_type: true
            }
            if have_type = false
            {
                ; An UNTYPED binding carries no item_type; its type is the
                ; collapsed initializer's. This is where the cast-declaration
                ; `let p allocate(...) as pointer[X]` surfaces.
                if binding.operation <> null
                {
                    if binding.operation.length = 1
                    {
                        let o_ptr binding.operation.get 0
                        if o_ptr <> null
                        {
                            set t: o_ptr.unwrap().result_type
                            set have_type: true
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            if have_type = false
                return
            if PointerCensus.is_pointer_shaped(t) = false
                return
            var pname String("")
            if binding.binding_item.name <> null
                set pname: String((*binding.binding_item.name))
            ; A fixed-size stack array (`var buf u8[64]`) is planned as a pointer
            ; with an array_size; its walk indexes in place and is the pure
            ; idiom (`tools/stackarray.py`'s class), so the kind names it.
            if t.array_size.get_length() > 0
            {
                var kb StringBuilder()
                kb.append "stack["
                kb.append t.array_size
                kb.append "]"
                loc_names.add(String^this(pname))
                loc_kinds.add(String^this(kb.to_string()))
            }
            else
                this.note_local(pname, binding.operation)
            this.record_named(binding.loc.start, "local", t, pname)
        }

        ; ================================================================
        ; Provenance of a buffer walk's base (`base=`) and the length in
        ; reach (`len=`). The class stays the same, so the union's dedupe
        ; and every count are untouched; only the detail grows.
        ; ================================================================

        ; Remember a pointer-typed local with the KIND of its initializer.
        procedure note_local(mutable this: PointerCensus, name: String, ops: ref[Vector[PlannedOperand]]?)
        {
            let kind this.initializer_kind(ops)
            loc_names.add(String^this(name))
            loc_kinds.add(String^this(kind))
        }

        function local_kind(this: PointerCensus, name: String) returns String
        {
            ; Latest declaration wins (a name may be re-bound in a later block).
            var i loc_names.length
            while i > 0
            {
                set i: i - 1
                let n loc_names.get i
                if n <> null
                    if (*n) = name
                    {
                        let k loc_kinds.get i
                        if k <> null
                            return String((*k))
                        return String("")
                    }
            }
            String("")
        }

        ; Index of `name` in the current body's parameters, or -1.
        function param_index(this: PointerCensus, name: String) returns int
        {
            if cur_params = null
                return 0 - 1
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < cur_params.length
            {
                let it cur_params.get i
                if it <> null
                {
                    let item it.unwrap()
                    if item.name <> null and (*item.name) = name
                        return i as int
                }
                set i: i + 1
            }
            0 - 1
        }

        function is_integer_type(t: PlannedType) returns bool
        {
            let n t.name
            if n = "int"
                return true
            if n = "uint"
                return true
            if n = "size_t"
                return true
            if n = "i8" or n = "i16" or n = "i32" or n = "i64" or n = "u8" or n = "u16" or n = "u32" or n = "u64"
                return true
            false
        }

        function item_is_integer(it: PlannedItem) returns bool
        {
            if it.item_type = null
                return false
            PointerCensus.is_integer_type((*it.item_type))
        }

        function item_name(it: PlannedItem) returns String
        {
            if it.name = null
                return String("")
            String((*it.name))
        }

        ; The length beside a pointer PARAMETER: the first integer parameter
        ; after it, else the first integer parameter anywhere, else "".
        function neighbour_length(this: PointerCensus, idx: int) returns String
        {
            if cur_params = null
                return String("")
            var i: size_t (idx + 1) as size_t
            while i < cur_params.length
            {
                let it cur_params.get i
                if it <> null and PointerCensus.item_is_integer(it.unwrap())
                    return PointerCensus.item_name(it.unwrap())
                set i: i + 1
            }
            set i: 0
            while i < cur_params.length
            {
                if (i as int) <> idx
                {
                    let it cur_params.get i
                    if it <> null
                        if PointerCensus.item_is_integer(it.unwrap())
                        {
                            var sb StringBuilder()
                            sb.append(PointerCensus.item_name(it.unwrap()))
                            sb.append "?"
                            return sb.to_string()
                        }
                }
                set i: i + 1
            }
            String("")
        }

        ; The planned structure behind a type, by mangled name first (an
        ; instantiation carries its own), then by bare name.
        function find_structure(this: PointerCensus, t: PlannedType) returns ref[PlannedStructure]?
        {
            if plan_structures = null
                return null
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < plan_structures.length
            {
                let sp plan_structures.get i
                if sp <> null and sp.unwrap().mangled_name = t.mangled_name
                    return sp
                set i: i + 1
            }
            set i: 0
            while i < plan_structures.length
            {
                let sp plan_structures.get i
                if sp <> null and sp.unwrap().name = t.name
                    return sp
                set i: i + 1
            }
            null
        }

        function name_says_length(n: String) returns bool
        {
            if n.contains(String("len"))
                return true
            if n.contains(String("size"))
                return true
            if n.contains(String("count")) or n.contains(String("cap")) or n = "n" or n.starts_with(String("n_"))
                return true
            false
        }

        ; `T.n` for the first integer field of T that reads like a length,
        ; else the first integer field, else "".
        function sibling_length(this: PointerCensus, t: PlannedType) returns String
        {
            let core PointerCensus.peel_option(t)
            let sp this.find_structure(core)
            if sp = null
                return String("")
            let st sp.unwrap()
            if st.properties = null
                return String("")
            var first String("")
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < st.properties.length
            {
                let pp st.properties.get i
                if pp <> null
                {
                    let prop pp.unwrap()
                    if PointerCensus.is_integer_type(prop.prop_type)
                    {
                        var sb StringBuilder()
                        sb.append st.name
                        sb.append "."
                        sb.append prop.name
                        let full sb.to_string()
                        if PointerCensus.name_says_length(prop.name)
                            return full
                        if first.get_length() = 0
                        {
                            var qb StringBuilder()
                            qb.append full
                            qb.append "?"
                            set first: qb.to_string()
                        }
                    }
                }
                set i: i + 1
            }
            first
        }

        function is_alloc_name(n: String) returns bool
        {
            if n = "allocate"
                return true
            if n = "allocate_oversized"
                return true
            if n = "malloc"
                return true
            if n = "calloc" or n = "realloc" or n = "aligned_alloc" or n = "scaly_aligned_alloc" or n = "mmap"
                return true
            false
        }

        ; The KIND of an operand, for a local's initializer: where the
        ; pointer came from. A cast is transparent -- it is the declaration,
        ; not the source.
        function operand_kind(this: PointerCensus, op: PlannedOperand) returns String
        {
            if op.member_access <> null
            {
                let ma op.member_access
                if ma.length > 0
                {
                    let last ma.get(ma.length - 1)
                    if last <> null
                    {
                        let hop last.unwrap()
                        var sb StringBuilder()
                        if hop.is_method
                            sb.append "call("
                        else
                            sb.append "field("
                        sb.append hop.parent_type.name
                        sb.append "."
                        sb.append hop.name
                        sb.append ")"
                        return sb.to_string()
                    }
                }
                return String("field")
            }
            choose op.expr
                when v: Variable
                {
                    var sb StringBuilder()
                    if this.param_index(v.name) >= 0
                        sb.append "param("
                    else
                        sb.append "local("
                    sb.append v.name
                    sb.append ")"
                    return sb.to_string()
                }
                when g: GlobalRef
                {
                    var sb StringBuilder()
                    sb.append "global("
                    sb.append g.name
                    sb.append ")"
                    return sb.to_string()
                }
                when c: Constant
                {
                    if PointerCensus.operand_is_null(op)
                        return String("null")
                    return String("const")
                }
                when call: Call
                {
                    if call.name = "*"
                        return String("deref")
                    if call.name = "&"
                        return String("addr")
                    if PointerCensus.arith_base(op) <> null
                        return String("arith")
                    if PointerCensus.is_alloc_name(call.name)
                        return String("alloc")
                    var sb StringBuilder()
                    sb.append "call("
                    sb.append call.name
                    sb.append ")"
                    return sb.to_string()
                }
                when as_expr: As
                {
                    if as_expr.value = null
                        return String("cast")
                    let r as_expr.value
                    return this.operand_kind((*r))
                }
                when bx: Box
                    return String("box")
                else
                    return String("other")
        }

        function initializer_kind(this: PointerCensus, ops: ref[Vector[PlannedOperand]]?) returns String
        {
            if ops = null
                return String("none")
            if ops.length <> 1
                return String("expr")
            let o ops.get 0
            if o = null
                return String("expr")
            this.operand_kind(o.unwrap())
        }

        ; Does the callee of `call` take a receiver (first param `this`)?
        function call_takes_this(this: PointerCensus, call: PlannedCall) returns bool
        {
            let callee this.find_function(call.mangled_name)
            if callee = null
                return false
            let cf callee.unwrap()
            if cf.input = null
                return false
            if cf.input.length = 0
                return false
            let first cf.input.get 0
            if first = null
                return false
            let fi first.unwrap()
            if fi.name = null
                return true
            (*fi.name) = "this"
        }

        ; ` base=... len=...` for the base of a buffer walk.
        function base_detail(this: PointerCensus, base: PlannedOperand) returns String
        {
            var sb StringBuilder()
            sb.append " base="
            var len String("")
            var kind_done false
            if base.member_access <> null
            {
                let ma base.member_access
                if ma.length > 0
                {
                    let last ma.get(ma.length - 1)
                    if last <> null
                    {
                        let hop last.unwrap()
                        ; A field walk names its concept's length; a method
                        ; result (`x.get_buffer() + i` as a member hop) the same.
                        set len: this.sibling_length(hop.parent_type)
                    }
                }
            }
            else
            {
                choose base.expr
                    when v: Variable
                    {
                        let idx this.param_index(v.name)
                        if idx >= 0
                            set len: this.neighbour_length(idx)
                        else
                        {
                            let k this.local_kind(v.name)
                            if k.get_length() > 0
                            {
                                sb.append "local("
                                sb.append v.name
                                sb.append "<-"
                                sb.append k
                                sb.append ")"
                                set kind_done: true
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    when call: Call
                    {
                        if call.args <> null
                            if call.args.length > 0
                                if this.call_takes_this(call)
                                {
                                    let a0 call.args.get 0
                                    if a0 <> null
                                    {
                                        let recv PointerCensus.peel_option(a0.unwrap().result_type)
                                        var rt recv
                                        ; Through a pointer/ref receiver: the pointee.
                                        if recv.name = "pointer"
                                            if recv.generics <> null
                                                if recv.generics.length = 1
                                                {
                                                    let g recv.generics.get 0
                                                    if g <> null
                                                        set rt: g.unwrap()
                                                }
                                        if recv.name = "ref"
                                            if recv.generics <> null
                                                if recv.generics.length = 1
                                                {
                                                    let g recv.generics.get 0
                                                    if g <> null
                                                        set rt: g.unwrap()
                                                }
                                        sb.append "call("
                                        sb.append call.name
                                        sb.append ") recv="
                                        sb.append rt.name
                                        set kind_done: true
                                        set len: this.sibling_length(rt)
                                    }
                                }
                    }
                    else
                        0
            }
            if kind_done = false
                sb.append(this.operand_kind(base))
            if len.get_length() > 0
            {
                sb.append " len="
                sb.append len
            }
            sb.to_string()
        }

        ; A buffer-walk site: class, type, then provenance.
        procedure record_walk(mutable this: PointerCensus, offset: size_t, cls: String, base: PlannedOperand)
        {
            let t base.result_type
            if this.is_handle(t)
            {
                set n_handle: n_handle + 1
                return
            }
            var sb StringBuilder()
            sb.append cls
            sb.append " "
            sb.append(Planner.get_readable_name(t))
            sb.append(this.base_detail(base))
            let text sb.to_string()
            let text_copy String^this(text)
            this.record(offset, cls, text_copy)
        }

        ; The pointer under `p + i` / `p - i`, or null when `op` is not that.
        function arith_base(op: PlannedOperand) returns ref[PlannedOperand]?
        {
            if op.member_access <> null
                return null
            choose op.expr
                when call: Call
                {
                    var is_arith false
                    if call.name = "+"
                        set is_arith: true
                    if call.name = "-"
                        set is_arith: true
                    if is_arith = false
                        return null
                    if call.args = null
                        return null
                    if call.args.length <> 2
                        return null
                    let lhs call.args.get 0
                    if lhs = null
                        return null
                    if PointerCensus.is_pointer_shaped(lhs.unwrap().result_type) = false
                        return null
                    return lhs
                }
                else
                    return null
        }

        ; The argument vector of `p + i` / `p - i` on a pointer, or null.
        function arith_args(op: PlannedOperand) returns ref[Vector[PlannedOperand]]?
        {
            if op.member_access <> null
                return null
            choose op.expr
                when call: Call
                {
                    var is_arith false
                    if call.name = "+"
                        set is_arith: true
                    if call.name = "-"
                        set is_arith: true
                    if is_arith = false
                        return null
                    if call.args = null
                        return null
                    if call.args.length <> 2
                        return null
                    let lhs call.args.get 0
                    if lhs = null
                        return null
                    if PointerCensus.is_pointer_shaped(lhs.unwrap().result_type) = false
                        return null
                    return call.args
                }
                else
                    return null
        }

        ; A string LITERAL, bare or under the planner's own cstr wrap
        ; (`coerce_string_args_to_cstr#` puts a synthetic PlannedAs over a
        ; literal bound for a `pointer[const_char]` parameter). Neither is a
        ; pointer the AUTHOR wrote, so neither is a site.
        function operand_is_string_literal(op: PlannedOperand) returns bool
        {
            if op.member_access <> null
                return false
            choose op.expr
                when c: Constant
                {
                    choose c.value
                        when sc: String
                            return true
                        else
                            return false
                }
                when as_expr: As
                {
                    if as_expr.value = null
                        return false
                    let r as_expr.value
                    PointerCensus.operand_is_string_literal((*r))
                }
                else
                    return false
        }

        function operand_is_null(op: PlannedOperand) returns bool
        {
            if op.member_access <> null
                return false
            choose op.expr
                when c: Constant
                {
                    choose c.value
                        when n: Null
                            return true
                        else
                            return false
                }
                else
                    return false
        }

        procedure find_operand(mutable this: PointerCensus, op: PlannedOperand)
        {
            choose op.expr
                when call: Call
                {
                    ; note_call answers true when it has walked the children
                    ; itself (the `*(p + i)` shape, reported as ONE site).
                    if this.note_call(op, call) = false
                        this.find_operands(call.args)
                }
                when as_expr: As
                {
                    if as_expr.value <> null
                    {
                        let r as_expr.value
                        let rv (*r)
                        var judge PointerCensus.is_pointer_shaped(as_expr.target_type)
                        if PointerCensus.operand_is_string_literal(rv)
                            set judge: false
                        ; A `String` VALUE handed to a cstr parameter is wrapped
                        ; the same way (`fopen(path, ...)` with a String path):
                        ; the planner's conversion, not an author's cast.
                        if rv.result_type.name = "String"
                            set judge: false
                        if judge
                        {
                            if this.is_handle(as_expr.target_type)
                            {
                                set n_handle: n_handle + 1
                                set judge: false
                            }
                        }
                        if judge
                        {
                            if PointerCensus.operand_is_null(rv)
                            {
                                this.record_typed(op.loc.start, "null-cast", as_expr.target_type)
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                var sb StringBuilder()
                                sb.append "cast "
                                sb.append(Planner.get_readable_name(rv.result_type))
                                sb.append " as "
                                sb.append(Planner.get_readable_name(as_expr.target_type))
                                let text sb.to_string()
                                let text_copy String^this(text)
                                this.record(op.loc.start, "cast", text_copy)
                            }
                        }
                        this.find_operand(rv)
                    }
                }
                when is_expr: Is
                {
                    if is_expr.value <> null
                    {
                        let r is_expr.value
                        let rv (*r)
                        if is_expr.is_null_check
                        {
                            if PointerCensus.is_pointer_shaped(rv.result_type)
                            {
                                this.record_typed(op.loc.start, "null-test", rv.result_type)
                            }
                        }
                        this.find_operand(rv)
                    }
                }
                when tp: Tuple
                {
                    if tp.components <> null
                    {
                        var i: size_t 0
                        while i < tp.components.length
                        {
                            let c_ptr tp.components.get i
                            if c_ptr <> null
                                this.find_operands(c_ptr.value)
                            set i: i + 1
                        }
                    }
                }
                when blk: Block
                {
                    if blk.statements <> null
                    {
                        var i: size_t 0
                        while i < blk.statements.length
                        {
                            let s_ptr blk.statements.get i
                            if s_ptr <> null
                                this.find_statement(s_ptr.unwrap())
                            set i: i + 1
                        }
                    }
                }
                when iff: If
                {
                    this.find_operands(iff.condition)
                    this.find_statement_ref(iff.consequent)
                    this.find_statement_ref(iff.alternative)
                }
                when mt: Match
                {
                    this.find_operands(mt.condition)
                    if mt.branches <> null
                    {
                        var i: size_t 0
                        while i < mt.branches.length
                        {
                            let br_ptr mt.branches.get i
                            if br_ptr <> null
                            {
                                let br (*br_ptr)
                                if br.cases <> null
                                {
                                    var ci: size_t 0
                                    while ci < br.cases.length
                                    {
                                        let cs_ptr br.cases.get ci
                                        if cs_ptr <> null
                                        {
                                            let cs (*cs_ptr)
                                            this.find_operands(cs.condition)
                                        }
                                        set ci: ci + 1
                                    }
                                }
                                this.find_statement_ref(br.consequent)
                            }
                            set i: i + 1
                        }
                    }
                    this.find_statement_ref(mt.alternative)
                }
                when ch: Choose
                {
                    this.find_operands(ch.condition)
                    if ch.cases <> null
                    {
                        var i: size_t 0
                        while i < ch.cases.length
                        {
                            let w_ptr ch.cases.get i
                            if w_ptr <> null
                            {
                                let w (*w_ptr)
                                this.find_statement_ref(w.consequent)
                            }
                            set i: i + 1
                        }
                    }
                    this.find_statement_ref(ch.alternative)
                }
                when fr: For
                {
                    this.find_operands(fr.expr)
                    this.find_action(fr.body)
                }
                when wh: While
                {
                    this.find_operands(wh.cond.operation)
                    this.find_action(wh.body)
                }
                when rp: Repeat
                    this.find_action(rp.body)
                when tr: Try
                {
                    this.find_operands(tr.cond.operation)
                    if tr.catches <> null
                    {
                        var i: size_t 0
                        while i < tr.catches.length
                        {
                            let w_ptr tr.catches.get i
                            if w_ptr <> null
                            {
                                let w (*w_ptr)
                                this.find_statement_ref(w.consequent)
                            }
                            set i: i + 1
                        }
                    }
                    this.find_statement_ref(tr.alternative)
                }
                when vc: VariantConstruction
                {
                    if vc.value <> null
                    {
                        let r vc.value
                        this.find_operand((*r))
                    }
                }
                when mx: Matrix
                {
                    if mx.operations <> null
                    {
                        var i: size_t 0
                        while i < mx.operations.length
                        {
                            let row_ptr mx.operations.get i
                            if row_ptr <> null
                                this.find_operands(row_ptr)
                            set i: i + 1
                        }
                    }
                }
                when bx: Box
                {
                    if bx.value <> null
                    {
                        let r bx.value
                        this.find_operand((*r))
                    }
                }
                else
                    0
        }

        ; The call-shaped sites: deref, arithmetic, null comparison, and a
        ; pointer handed to a callee.
        procedure note_call(mutable this: PointerCensus, op: PlannedOperand, call: PlannedCall) returns bool
        {
            if call.args = null
                return false
            let argc call.args.length
            if call.name = "*"
            {
                if argc = 1
                {
                    let a_ptr call.args.get 0
                    if a_ptr <> null
                    {
                        let a (*a_ptr)
                        ; `*(p + i)` first: the sum is pointer-typed too, so
                        ; asked second it would read as a plain deref.
                        let inner_args PointerCensus.arith_args(a)
                        if inner_args <> null
                        {
                            let base inner_args.get 0
                            if base <> null
                            {
                                this.record_walk(op.loc.start, "deref-arith", base.unwrap())
                            }
                            this.find_operands(inner_args)
                            return true
                        }
                        if PointerCensus.is_pointer_shaped(a.result_type)
                        {
                            this.record_typed(op.loc.start, "deref", a.result_type)
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            if PointerCensus.is_optional_ref(a.result_type)
                                set n_optref_deref: n_optref_deref + 1
                        }
                    }
                    return false
                }
            }
            var is_arith false
            if call.name = "+"
                set is_arith: true
            if call.name = "-"
                set is_arith: true
            if is_arith
            {
                if argc = 2
                {
                    let inner PointerCensus.arith_base(op)
                    if inner <> null
                    {
                        this.record_walk(op.loc.start, "arith", inner.unwrap())
                    }
                    return false
                }
            }
            var is_eq false
            if call.name = "="
                set is_eq: true
            if call.name = "<>"
                set is_eq: true
            if is_eq
            {
                if argc = 2
                {
                    let l_ptr call.args.get 0
                    let r_ptr call.args.get 1
                    if l_ptr <> null
                    {
                        if r_ptr <> null
                        {
                            let l (*l_ptr)
                            let r (*r_ptr)
                            var tested: ref[PlannedOperand]? null
                            if PointerCensus.operand_is_null(r)
                                set tested: l_ptr
                            if PointerCensus.operand_is_null(l)
                                set tested: r_ptr
                            if tested <> null
                            {
                                let t tested.unwrap().result_type
                                if PointerCensus.is_pointer_shaped(t)
                                {
                                    this.record_typed(op.loc.start, "null-test", t)
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    return false
                }
            }
            if call.name = "&"
                return false
            if call.is_operator
                return false
            ; Arguments, judged against the callee's DECLARED parameters.
            let callee this.find_function(call.mangled_name)
            var params: ref[Vector[PlannedItem]]? null
            var resolved false
            var takes_this false
            ; A CONSTRUCTION's arguments carry no receiver while the
            ; initializer's `input` starts with `this`: params are read one
            ; slot ahead. Measured before this: 25 `pointer[u32]` hazards in
            ; opensp, every one `InputSource(origin, contents, length)` with
            ; the buffer read against the `origin` parameter.
            var is_init false
            var param_shift: size_t 0
            var callee_extern false
            if call.name = "init"
                set is_init: true
            var callee_name String(call.name)
            if callee <> null
            {
                let cf callee.unwrap()
                set callee_name: String(cf.name)
                set resolved: true
                ; An initializer is recorded in plan.functions too (named
                ; `init`, with `this` first), so it resolves HERE before the
                ; structure table is asked: the construction shape is decided
                ; by the name, not by which table answered.
                if cf.name = "init"
                {
                    set is_init: true
                    ; Name the constructed type: `Source.init`, not `init`.
                    var nb StringBuilder()
                    nb.append call.result_type.name
                    nb.append ".init"
                    set callee_name: nb.to_string()
                }
                if PointerCensus.fn_is_body(cf) = false
                    set callee_extern: true
                set params: cf.input
            }
            else
            {
                let ini this.find_initializer(call.mangled_name)
                if ini <> null
                {
                    set resolved: true
                    set is_init: true
                    set params: ini.unwrap().input
                    var nb StringBuilder()
                    nb.append call.result_type.name
                    nb.append ".init"
                    set callee_name: nb.to_string()
                }
                else
                {
                    if this.is_extern_name(call.mangled_name)
                    {
                        set resolved: true
                        set callee_extern: true
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        ; A construction whose initializer this root does not
                        ; hold (a dependency's `String(ptr, len)`): name the
                        ; constructed type so the line reads `String.init`.
                        if call.name = "init"
                        {
                            var nb StringBuilder()
                            nb.append call.result_type.name
                            nb.append ".init"
                            set callee_name: nb.to_string()
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            if params <> null
            {
                if params.length > 0
                {
                    let first params.get 0
                    if first <> null
                    {
                        let fi first.unwrap()
                        ; The receiver item is `this`, or carries no name at
                        ; all (Array.reallocate's does, measured).
                        if fi.name = null
                            set takes_this: true
                        else
                            if (*fi.name) = "this"
                                set takes_this: true
                    }
                }
            }
            if is_init
                if takes_this
                {
                    set takes_this: false
                    set param_shift: 1
                }
            var i: size_t 0
            while i < argc
            {
                var skip false
                if i = 0 and takes_this
                    set skip: true
                let a_ptr call.args.get i
                if a_ptr = null
                    set skip: true
                if skip = false
                {
                    let a (*a_ptr)
                    ; The declared parameter behind this argument, if known.
                    var have_param false
                    var param_type: PlannedType PointerCensus.void_type()
                    var param_name String("")
                    if params <> null
                    {
                        if i + param_shift < params.length
                        {
                            let it_ptr params.get(i + param_shift)
                            if it_ptr <> null
                            {
                                let it it_ptr.unwrap()
                                if it.item_type <> null
                                {
                                    set param_type: (*it.item_type)
                                    set have_param: true
                                }
                                if it.name <> null
                                    set param_name: String((*it.name))
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    var where StringBuilder()
                    where.append " -> "
                    where.append callee_name
                    if have_param
                    {
                        where.append "("
                        where.append param_name
                        where.append ")"
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        where.append "["
                        where.append(Planner.size_to_string(i))
                        where.append "]"
                    }
                    let where_str where.to_string()

                    var judge PointerCensus.is_pointer_shaped(a.result_type)
                    if PointerCensus.operand_is_string_literal(a)
                        set judge: false
                    if PointerCensus.operand_is_this(a)
                        set judge: false
                    ; A bare `null` types as pointer[void]; into an Option
                    ; parameter it is the language's own spelling, not a site.
                    if PointerCensus.operand_is_null(a)
                        set judge: false
                    if judge
                    {
                        if this.is_handle(a.result_type)
                        {
                            set n_handle: n_handle + 1
                            set judge: false
                        }
                    }
                    if judge
                    {
                        var cls String("arg")
                        if resolved = false
                            set cls: String("arg-unresolved")
                        if callee_extern
                            set cls: String("arg-extern")
                        if have_param and callee_extern = false and PointerCensus.is_ref_shaped(param_type)
                            set cls: String("h-pointer-into-ref")
                        var sb StringBuilder()
                        sb.append cls
                        sb.append " "
                        sb.append(Planner.get_readable_name(a.result_type))
                        sb.append where_str
                        let text sb.to_string()
                        let text_copy String^this(text)
                        this.record(a.loc.start, cls, text_copy)
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        ; A Slice where the callee declared a pointer: rc 0,
                        ; the callee reads the struct as its buffer.
                        if have_param
                            if a.result_type.name = "Slice"
                                if PointerCensus.is_pointer_shaped(param_type)
                                {
                                    var sb StringBuilder()
                                    sb.append "h-slice-into-pointer "
                                    sb.append(Planner.get_readable_name(a.result_type))
                                    sb.append where_str
                                    let text sb.to_string()
                                    let text_copy String^this(text)
                                    this.record(a.loc.start, "h-slice-into-pointer", text_copy)
                                }
                    }
                }
                set i: i + 1
            }
            false
        }
    }
}
